A||N||5||ricksmastermix||Held Motorsports Suspension info.||||1||
Z||000000||ricksmastermix||11-23-2001||12:24 PM||||I'm considering the Held Motorsports (Formerly Rayne Motorsports) Bumpsteer Upgrade and their Wide-Track Sport Suspension upgrade. Anybody out there had experience with these kits? How effective are the modifications?<BR>Also, planning a brake upgrade and an engine swap (3.4l TDC V-6.) Any input would be appreciated.<BR>Rick||||reg||1
Z||000001||DKOV||11-23-2001||01:59 PM||||I am in that very process now.  I've completed the 3.4 conversion to my 88 GT and have Held's HUGE 13 inch brake kit.  The suspension is in process now so I can't tell you how it "handles" quite yet, but if it performs at all like their other components, it is WORTH it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Don't forget your AXELS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||11-23-2001||04:14 PM||||Held's stuff is top-notch, however!<P>You will be FAR FAR FAR better off just swapping to an 88 cradle in the rear of your car! <P>The front suspension has several geometry fixes, including inherant coil-over-love  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>It's ideal (and might be nessicary on early chassis?) for Held's 13" 4-pot brake upgrade.<P>Toss all this together, mix with a 3.4TDC (DKOV can tell you how to HOT ROD that motor for even more power!) and you've got one very fun 7,000rpm Fiero!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||DKOV||11-23-2001||05:05 PM||||About those brakes... if your Fiero is NOT an 88 you will also need the spindle drop for everything to fit right.  Both the slolam and the wide track setups work with the big brakes and spindle drop combo.  If your car IS an 88, the stock spindles work fine.<P>I went with the coil-over setup for my car as well.  I currently have a 1.5 inch drop on it as well.  Looks INCREDIBLE.<P>As for the 3.4 swap... Better get a NECK BRACE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
